    "## Two preprocessing representations\n",
    "\n",
    "Only the two requested preprocessing methods are prepared:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Distance-to-stroke:** converts each pixel into an exponentially decaying response based on its distance from the nearest stroke.\n",
    "- **Local-density blur:** replaces each pixel with the local mean stroke density in a square neighbourhood.\n",
    "\n",
    "The preprocessing arrays are stored as `uint8` values from 0 to 255 to reduce memory use. They are converted back to floating-point values from 0 to 1 when supplied to the CNN. This storage encoding does not alter the synthetic source rasters or vector labels."
   ]
  },
